Turns off two rules. The pin was found needing both off; at its current seed
the second alone fails it and the first alone does not. The in-flight occupant
rule of f566b64 (Look at an occupant of a marked path while its want is in
flight) is undone: FolderState::scanned again ignores every observation of a
path whose want is in flight, marked or not, so an occupant at a marked path
no longer clears the mark while its restoring want is wanted, fetching or
committing. And a deny no longer waits while a path of its held item carries
the restoring mark: the Restoring branch of the deny arm of
FolderState::unsettled, added by f6cff50 (Queue deny and revert until the
folder settles), is removed. DESIGN.md §8.3, and §7.5's revert exception.

